<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bhupatindra Malla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1696–1722</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bhupatindra Malla was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhaktapur">Bhaktapur</a>, one of the three Newar kingdoms of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathmandu-valley">Kathmandu Valley</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>. A great builder, he raised the five-storey Nyatapola temple in 1702, the tallest pagoda in the valley, and enlarged the royal palace of fifty-five windows. His statue on a pillar still faces the palace in Bhaktapur's Durbar Square.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bhupatindra-malla.jpg" alt="Bhupatindra Malla" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nyeta · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhupatindra_Malla_painting_form_the_18th_century.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
